/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Problem Statement  The increased reliance on digital screens among Indian children, especially post-COVID, has blurred the line between healthy and excessive screen use. Many children are spending extended hours on recreational screen activities, often exceeding recommended limits. This raises concerns about long-term health outcomes, such as poor sleep, anxiety, and eye strain. Despite this, there is limited visibility into which age groups, genders, or regions are most at risk, and whether screen time is being used productively or not.)
/E (Problem Statement  The increased reliance on digital screens among Indian children, especially post-COVID, has blurred the line between healthy and excessive screen use. Many children are spending extended hours on recreational screen activities, often exceeding recommended limits. This raises concerns about long-term health outcomes, such as poor sleep, anxiety, and eye strain. Despite this, there is limited visibility into which age groups, genders, or regions are most at risk, and whether screen time is being used productively or not.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
